    bodyMarkdown: "## Definitions\n\n| **Term**                             | **Definition**                                                                                                              |\n|--------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Cannabis Supplier                    | A company that supplies cannabis materials (e.g., biomass, distillate); must be state-licensed.                             |\n| Non-Cannabis Supplier                | A company supplying material that affects the finished good but is not cannabis (e.g., ingredients, cartridges, packaging). |\n| Service Supplier                     | A company supplying a service vital to operations (e.g., pest control, laboratory testing, calibration).                    |\n| Certificate of Analysis / Conformity | Documentation that a material conforms to requirements (lot number, manufacturing/expiration date, product name).           |\n| Approved Supplier                    | A supplier that has met qualification requirements and is authorized for use.                                               |\n\n## Associated Documents / References\n\n- Suppliers and Supplier Qualification records in CannaQMS\n\n- Incoming Inspection SOP\n\n- Michigan Administrative Code R 420.xxx; ISO/IEC 17025 (laboratories)\n\n## Responsibilities\n\n| **Role**                    | **Responsibility**                                                                                  |\n|-----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Executive / Management      | Approves suppliers and determines which reputable vendors to use.                                   |\n| Quality                     | Owns supplier qualification and re-qualification and maintains certificates and status in CannaQMS. |\n| Department Lead / Warehouse | Performs incoming inspection of received cannabis and non-cannabis material.                        |\n\n## Procedure\n\n1.  **Supplier qualification**\n\n- Suppliers are qualified in CannaQMS before use. The evidence required depends on the supplier type; qualification status and expiry are tracked with re-qualification alerts.\n\n2.  **Cannabis material suppliers**\n\n- Must be licensed by the State of Michigan as a cultivator or producer.\n\n3.  **Non-cannabis material suppliers**\n\n- Provide a Certificate of Analysis or Conformity showing the material conforms to applicable requirements (lot number, manufacturing/expiration date, product name). Off-the-shelf items (cones, cartridges, mouthpieces) come from reputable, approved vendors.\n\n4.  **Laboratory (testing) suppliers**\n\n- Must be accredited to ISO/IEC 17025 for the required safety tests and recognized/approved by the State of Michigan.\n\n5.  **Critical service suppliers**\n\n- Pest control, testing, and calibration providers must show evidence of conformity to applicable regulations. Pest control also provides Safety Data Sheets for chemicals used, a facility map of trap locations, and the service provider's signature and date. Calibration providers conform to ISO/IEC 17025 or equivalent.\n\n6.  **Non-critical / indirect suppliers**\n\n- Selected on business merit (turnaround time, cost, service) — e.g., kettles, ovens, utensils.\n\n7.  **Records and re-qualification**\n\n- Supplier records, certificates, and qualification status are maintained in CannaQMS; received material is verified per the Incoming Inspection SOP.\n\n## Change History\n\n| **Revision** | **Description of Change** | **Release Date** |\n|--------------|---------------------------|------------------|\n| A            | New document              | [ ]            |",
