    bodyMarkdown: "## Definitions\n\n| **Term**                         | **Definition**                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n|----------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Cannabis Regulatory Agency (CRA) | The agency administering Michigan's cannabis regulations (Marihuana Rules).                                                                                                                                               |\n| Field Action                     | Actions required on product that has been released for sale or is in the distribution chain.                                                                                                                              |\n| Recall                           | A mandatory, regulatory-driven removal of product from the market due to a defect, contamination, labeling error, or other risk to consumer safety; involves notifying authorities and the public and retrieving product. |\n| Withdrawal                       | A voluntary removal of product with no immediate health risk (e.g., non-compliance or quality/commercial reasons); may not require public notification.                                                                   |\n| Field Action Letter              | An approved communication to affected parties/public describing the issue and the actions required of them.                                                                                                               |\n| Field Action Plan / Report       | A cross-functional document defining the affected product, required actions, closure tracking and criteria, and the date the CRA was notified of closure.                                                                 |\n\n## Associated Documents / References\n\n- Field Action records in CannaQMS\n\n- Quality Issues Management SOP; Cannabis Destruction Procedure; Packaging & Labeling requirements\n\n- Michigan Administrative Code R 420.xxx (field actions / recalls)\n\n## Responsibilities\n\n| **Role**              | **Responsibility**                                                                                                                                                      |\n|-----------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Executive Team        | Authorizes the field action, communicates regular updates to the CRA, and determines final product disposition.                                                         |\n| Field Action Team     | Cross-functional group (Compliance/Regulatory, Quality, Production, Distribution/Logistics, Sales/Retail, Marketing, Legal, Finance) that builds and executes the plan. |\n| Quality / Compliance  | Coordinates the action, maintains records, and manages CRA notifications.                                                                                               |\n| Operations Management | Assists the Executive Team in building and executing the action plan.                                                                                                   |\n\n## Procedure\n\n1.  **Trigger and risk assessment**\n\n- A field action is initiated upon awareness of an issue from an internal finding, a complaint, or a CRA request.\n\n- Assess the health/safety risk to classify the action as a Recall (mandatory, safety) or a Withdrawal (voluntary, no immediate risk).\n\n2.  **Open the field action**\n\n- Open a Field Action in CannaQMS recording the affected product (Metrc number, batch, manufacturing details), the reason, and the classification.\n\n3.  **Field action plan**\n\n- The cross-functional Field Action Team develops a plan covering the actions required of customers/retail/distribution/transport, how closure will be tracked, and the criteria for assuming closure.\n\n4.  **Notifications**\n\n- Notify the CRA in accordance with Michigan requirements and provide regular updates on progress.\n\n- Issue an approved Field Action Letter to affected parties and, where required, the public.\n\n5.  **Retrieval and disposition**\n\n- Retrieve and quarantine affected product from the field/distribution chain.\n\n- Determine and document the final disposition; destruction is performed per the Cannabis Destruction Procedure.\n\n6.  **Closure**\n\n- Track completion against the closure criteria and record the date the CRA was notified of closure.\n\n- Capture corrective actions to prevent recurrence; open a linked CAPA where appropriate.\n\n7.  **Records**\n\n- All field-action records are retained in CannaQMS per the record-retention policy.\n\n## Change History\n\n| **Revision** | **Description of Change** | **Release Date** |\n|--------------|---------------------------|------------------|\n| A            | New document              | [ ]            |",
